Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: airoha: program the SCU XSI selection before bringup

pcs_pre_config() is only reached through phylink_major_config(), which
does not repeat once an MLO_AN_PHY link has settled: gdm4 has a
phy-handle, the interface stays 2500BASE-X for the whole uptime, so
airoha_pcs_setup_scu() runs at most once, at phylink start, before the
PHY has brought the lane up.

Consequence on hardware: AIROHA_SCU_SSR3 (0x1fa20094) keeps
ETH_XSI_SEL = 0, the SerDes lane is not routed to the HSGMII PCS and
the receiver sees no signal at all:

  pcs_pma DIG_RO_RESERVE_2 (0x1fa7b380) RX_SIGDET = 0

Writing ETH_XSI_SEL = AIROHA_SCU_ETH_XSI_HSGMII (0x4000) by hand flips
RX_SIGDET to 1 immediately, which proves the SCU selection is the
missing piece and that the lane itself is healthy.

pcs_config() runs on every phylink start, so program the SCU there as
well, ahead of the analog bringup: the PLL/CDR calibration depends on
the lane actually being routed.

Signed-off-by: local

--- a/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/airoha/pcs-airoha-common.c
@@ -467,9 +467,19 @@ static int airoha_pcs_config(struct phylink_pcs *pcs, unsigned int neg_mode,
 	maps = &priv->maps[port->index];
 	port->interface = interface;
 	data = priv->data;
 
+	/*
+	 * phylink only runs ->pcs_pre_config() from phylink_major_config(),
+	 * which does not repeat for a settled MLO_AN_PHY link.  ETH_XSI_SEL
+	 * then stays 0, the SerDes lane is never routed to this PCS,
+	 * RX_SIGDET reads 0 and nothing is received even though the copper
+	 * side reports link up.  Program the SCU here too, and before the
+	 * analog bringup so the PLL/CDR calibration runs already routed.
+	 */
+	airoha_pcs_setup_scu(priv, port->index, interface);
+
 	/* Apply Analog and Digital configuration for PCS */
 	if (data->bringup) {
 		ret = data->bringup(priv, index, interface);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
